# Requests for poking the API by hand, from an editor.
#
# Every one of these is a GET, because every route that touches ERP data is.
# The two exceptions -- signing in and choosing a customer -- change this
# application's own session and are included so the whole surface is here.

@host = http://127.0.0.1:5080

### Is it awake, and what does it think it is pointed at
GET {{host}}/health
Accept: application/json

### Alive, without consulting anything
GET {{host}}/health/live
Accept: application/json

### Search the catalogue
GET {{host}}/api/v1/parts?q=breaker&limit=10
Accept: application/json

### One part, every branch, and the list price
GET {{host}}/api/v1/parts/S-BRK00000/availability
Accept: application/json

### The same part, priced for a customer
GET {{host}}/api/v1/parts/S-BRK00000/availability?customerAccount=C-10000
Accept: application/json

### What is holding a branch's committed stock
GET {{host}}/api/v1/parts/S-BRK00000/commitments?branchCode=DEN
Accept: application/json

### The record as the ERP stores it, separators and all
GET {{host}}/api/v1/parts/S-BRK00000/record
Accept: application/json

### Customers, for the selector
GET {{host}}/api/v1/customers?q=front
Accept: application/json

### Who is signed in
GET {{host}}/api/v1/session
Accept: application/json

### The demonstration personas on offer
GET {{host}}/api/v1/session/personas
Accept: application/json

### What this person has asked of the system
GET {{host}}/api/v1/activity?limit=20
Accept: application/json

### Become a different persona. Not a login; there is no password.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/session
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subject": "demo|marcus" }

### Choose the customer being served
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/session/customer
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerAccount": "C-10000" }
